{"availability":"available","full":"rolandbrake/pilang","name":"pilang","description":"Pilang is a lightweight, general-purpose programming language written in C. a full real-world scripting language with modular architecture, standard library support, and operating system integration.","category":"Education","language":"C","stars":10,"forks":0,"created":"2026-02-22T14:39:41Z","updated":"2026-10-10T09:58:01Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://pi-lang.netlify.app/","topics":["c","javascript","machine-learning","mathematics","neural","neural-networks","programming-language","python","tensors"],"demo":"https://pi-lang.netlify.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T11:06:59.783Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T11:06:59.783Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T11:06:59.783Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T11:06:59.783Z","stars":10,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A compact language for turning data, math, and ideas into visible experiments.","Pilang is for the moment when an idea is still small enough to explore: shape some data, transform it, run the math, and draw the result without assembling a stack of packages first. It is a C-powered scripting language with tensors, image processing, 2D charts, and interactive 3D plots in its core modules.","Its syntax keeps expressive operations close to the data. Build ranges and comprehensions, slice in either direction, use # for length, spread values with ..., and send a value through a pipeline with =>. The result is a language that reads naturally while staying playful and direct for numerical work, simulations, and visual experiments."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rolandbrake/pilang/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"3f0adf4187d7372419a710f4d45b1ea168af0435a361aa24a29b6c58a0ef25c2","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T11:06:59.890Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T11:06:59.890Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoe